{"chapter-slug":"rw8-25 KH","paragraph":718,"wording":"[Gladiators]","event":"named","holder-slug":"yvlon-byres","holder-quote":"It cost money to feed and house them, and that was a luxury most didn’t have. A [Bandit] normally got the noose. However, Chandrar put their prisoners to work. They made slaves out of them or—as Yvlon now knew intimately—made them [Gladiators].","id":"85805ca2-a5ae-51be-b3ca-fe52fdccbd82"}
{"chapter-slug":"rw8-25 KH","paragraph":739,"wording":"[Gladiators]","event":"named","claimed":true,"claimed-by-slug":"Rexes","holder-quote":"The female [Thief] shivered. Her name was Rexes, and she was a Cotton-caste [Thief]. Her strings were frayed, but she had old, silk arms, which made them fast—too bad her legs hadn’t been as fast, or she wouldn’t have been caught.","id":"ddced4de-e719-53a9-ae7c-7cdc665590be"}
